l component) and to an assumed `RHOAI Observability`\n101\t  team (grounded in the strategy's `observability` label). Both need human\n102\t  confirmation — see Health Warnings.\n103\t- **E003/E004 (HLR-3 split)**: HLR-3 names \"KServe controller and serving\n104\t  runtimes\". `KServe` and `Serving Runtimes` are separate canonical components,\n105\t  so the work is split: the controller (KServe) and the model-serving runtimes\n106\t  (Serving Runtimes). Both assigned to RHOAI Serving, the owning team in\n107\t  `architecture-context/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md`, which also documents the serving\n108\t  runtimes (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit) as part of the serving stack.\n109\t- **Serving Runtimes** has no dedicated file under\n110\t  `.context/architecture-context/` but is documented inside\n111\t  `architecture-context/rhoai-3.0/kserve.md` as an in-platform dependency\n112\t  (vLLM, OpenVINO, Caikit for model execution). It is therefore treated as\n113\t  in-platform and gets a normal adoption epic — no repo/konflux onboarding\n114\t  chain is generated.\n115\t- **Adoption epic teams** are taken from each component's architecture-context\n116\t  owning team (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, KServe/Serving Runtimes → RHOAI\n117\t  Serving, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines, Model Registry → Model\n118\t  Registry, TrustyAI → TrustyAI, Notebooks → Workbenches, Training Operator →\n119\t  Distributed Workloads), because the strategy has no Impacted Teams table.\n120\t\n121\t## Health Warnings\n122\t\n123\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n124\t  Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then Acceptance Criteria, and no\n125\t  Non-Functional Requirements. Teams were inferred from architecture context;\n126\t  acceptance criteria below are derived from the HLRs. Non-blocking, but the\n127\t  epic ACs should be sanity-checked by the component teams.\n128\t- **Unowned convention work (HLR-1)**: no team is named for authoring the\n129\t  platfo