on of the correlation id.\n50\t- Publish the convention at a location accessible to all adopting component\n51\t  teams.\n52\t- Socialize the convention with the adopting component teams so adoption can\n53\t  proceed (review of the draft, not per-component implementation).\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A JSON schema for the log format is published and validates example records\n58\t  from each of Go, Python, and TypeScript.\n59\t- Every record conforming to the schema carries the required fields:\n60\t  timestamp, level, component, namespace, correlation id.\n61\t- Library guidance exists for Go, Python, and TypeScript, each demonstrating\n62\t  emission of a schema-conformant record.\n63\t- The convention document is published and reachable by all adopting component\n64\t  teams.\n65\t- The convention has been reviewed by representatives of the adopting\n66\t  component teams with no unresolved objections to the required-field set.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- HLR-1 (P0): A platform logging convention is published: JSON schema,\n71\t  required fields (timestamp, level, component, namespace, correlation id),\n72\t  and library guidance per language (Go, Python, TypeScript).\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a52c16f88ac64be","agent_id":"a4cfa454365ef8824","session_id":"58dc5346-ca06-4598-877d-d8e47ba1db78","uuid":"1d0c07cd-0350-416a-8abc-4a47d3fa1246","timestamp":"2026-10-22T18:19:14.567Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a7d642ae0ae2fe8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9011 decomposition"}
